{"title":"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Sin-Cos_Angle_Addition)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Sin-Cos Angle Addition)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Root_Approximation,_No_Trig_Identities)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Root Approximation, No Trig Identities)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Very_Fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Very Fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_MadMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by MadMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An analog clock starts at midnight and runs for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> minutes before stopping. What is the tangent of the acute angle between the hour hand and the minute hand when the clock stops?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/9441b22185ada083a53c101f0f63b494af9800a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\sqrt{2}-1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 2-\\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 3-\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"514\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, with a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d13da0a9675ed419cb44e4c3a8be7f3f226dad11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" />, the clock is now at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d5519fdc63d96b5aa59714c0755969ed7293846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9:45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>At this time, the hour is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e126f0d41c904d37ba2c332347a24b75d4ac3066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> over, so the hour hand is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e126f0d41c904d37ba2c332347a24b75d4ac3066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the way between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. There is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/183986ef22f441197c7585c1ffec5c724f8f51d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{360^{\\circ}}{12} = 30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"39\" /> angle between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and since the hour hand is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e126f0d41c904d37ba2c332347a24b75d4ac3066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the way, it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/2/11268268fa2ce57143c3a62a3e163d13b0022582.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{45}{2}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"40\" /> from the minute hand, which is pointing directly at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We now just need to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/52528a865cc8f6733811518d4d44fcf2b06e1c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(\\frac{45}{2}^{\\circ}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"87\" height=\"45\" />, so let this be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Using the tangent addition formula, we find that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/444f8d9dd9d895a3ac3a8af631786693377c1c13.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}&amp;\\tan\\left(45^{\\circ}\\right) = \\frac{x + x}{1 - x\\cdot x} \\\\ &amp;\\iff 1 = \\frac{2x}{1-x^2} \\\\  &amp;\\iff x^2+2x-1 = 0.\\end{align*}\" width=\"178\" height=\"104\" />\nUsing the quadratic formula, and knowing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be positive since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8cee028c7eef18d21b196bcaad56346afd8aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^{\\circ} &lt; \\frac{45}{2}^{\\circ} &lt; 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"123\" height=\"40\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/7/2f70a00e79c2d04f29475feb2c59b792dd5f71b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\tan\\left(\\frac{45}{2}^{\\circ}\\right) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } \\sqrt{2}-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"248\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>~lprado\n</p><p><br />\nNote: One could solve this quickly using the <i>tangent half-angle identity</i>, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/2/862fe7692ec2f363f405850bbf9f14049bc3761d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right) = \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{1+\\cos(\\theta)} = \\frac{1-\\cos(\\theta)}{\\sin(\\theta)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"284\" height=\"45\" />. ~math660\n</p><p><br />\nNote: Another interesting way to find the angle between the hands at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d5519fdc63d96b5aa59714c0755969ed7293846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9:45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is to use the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/d/7ddba364dfb654b1343bfd32763c56837a05aed9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(30h - \\frac{11}{2}m\\right)^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"125\" height=\"46\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the hour and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is the minute. In this case, we deduce that the angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a103a57d36811120138b6907bc2e33e42a5d53c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(30 \\cdot 9 - \\frac{11}{2} \\cdot 45\\right)^{\\circ} = \\left(\\frac{540-495}{2}\\right)^{\\circ} = \\frac{45}{2}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"345\" height=\"46\" />, as desired. ~lprado\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Sin-Cos_Angle_Addition.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Sin-Cos_Angle_Addition)\">Solution 2 (Sin-Cos Angle Addition)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Sin-Cos Angle Addition)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The closest multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80ba0021a6b63220ca342f779478c54c36a3b914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60 \\cdot 33 = 1980$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, leaves remainder <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and thus the clock depicts hour <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d438c26afafe8e064ad56928d94605b4caf1f2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025 - 1980 = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" /> minutes, so the time is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d5519fdc63d96b5aa59714c0755969ed7293846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9:45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. As an hour has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes, this represents <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/7/cd790f6b93dafdc37ff001d9245e88ca48e5e08d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{45}{60} = 0.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" /> of an hour past the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th hour. \n</p><p>The angle between two successive hours on the clock face is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/183986ef22f441197c7585c1ffec5c724f8f51d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{360^{\\circ}}{12} = 30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"39\" />, so from above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/6/ed613705321d3d1f1b28263026d842c70c5667b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.75 \\cdot 30^{\\circ} = 22.5^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" />. Since double <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/8/b6821c7f2896abf329848bfff7fbde004fc25f65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22.5^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821d3f11ab7a3e93c7a404a34224228f0449505a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, we can use sine and cosine double angle (or addition) identities:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a25e344b74df0554400c7bb91906189fbff3db3b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(2 \\theta)=\\sin(\\theta)\\cdot\\cos(\\theta)+\\sin(\\theta)\\cdot\\cos(\\theta)=2 \\sin(\\theta)\\cos(\\theta)\\]\" width=\"444\" height=\"18\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80c28a18ec15cb92bf6de88e1ff4fb27a0417f15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(2 \\theta)=\\cos(\\theta)\\cdot\\cos(\\theta)-\\sin(\\theta)\\cdot\\sin(\\theta)=\\cos^2(\\theta)-\\sin^2(\\theta).\\]\" width=\"472\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Notice that by dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0d01d6feeacd3654d74a817ddd486784fdddb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(2 \\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738641ab6fb64d3695f38ff428ca84a6a90d4708.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(2 \\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, the denominator and numerator cancel a trig function, so we obtain\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/f/8bf418f880bf76d811b4679e01a47dac6601ce53.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\cos(2 \\theta)}{\\sin(2 \\theta)} = \\frac{\\cos^2(\\theta)-\\sin^2(\\theta)}{2 \\sin(\\theta)\\cos(\\theta)},\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"45\" /> which reduces to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b7ac4a07da36a116d7138b1cfc07965b358fc32.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2}{\\tan(2 \\theta)} = \\frac{\\cos(\\theta)}{\\sin(\\theta)} - \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{\\cos(\\theta)}.\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Now setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20b20a1df3146c3efbc2520ca7f3580b4a1fcdeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = 22.5^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />, and recalling that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/9/6c91c59459d0ba9394a9e37e3073e12cdeb15894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(45^{\\circ}\\right) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />, we deduce that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19dfce3dec308eacd4e0ea9b6a68e0428f649763.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 = \\frac{1}{\\tan\\left(22.5^{\\circ}\\right)} - \\tan\\left(22.5^{\\circ}\\right).\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f84c47183e158d3a6a189925a00dca14587a07d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\tan\\left(22.5^{\\circ}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" /> and using the quadratic formula, this becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/d/15dae40cc53bb239f7de3c33207ba63fb0ae3c6f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x = 1 - x^2 \\iff x^2 + 2x - 1 = 0 \\iff x = \\frac{-2\\pm\\sqrt{4+4}}{2} = \\pm\\sqrt{2} - 1.\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"40\" />\nBut we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae4fd68f44ac9b909f8d91f9d498de5759bb45b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/6/62618d6f4f83fa87707c6083d91db46e9eb351c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^{\\circ} &lt; 22.5^{\\circ} &lt; 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" />, and thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/f/d9f637ebbab0c4cfabb4f95699eb768c6d802765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } \\sqrt{2}-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"138\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>~tebby\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Root_Approximation.2C_No_Trig_Identities.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Root_Approximation,_No_Trig_Identities)\">Solution 3 (Root Approximation, No Trig Identities)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Root Approximation, No Trig Identities)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Following from Solutions 1 and 2, we get the time to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d5519fdc63d96b5aa59714c0755969ed7293846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9:45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and the angle between the hour and minute hands to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/8/b6821c7f2896abf329848bfff7fbde004fc25f65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22.5^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Moreover, we know that this angle satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56a6b2c0fbd83940ff6e4b634690f6e3ecd3e556.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22.5^{\\circ} &lt; 30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/48868d46ab1b757b674922243394e1c868465a65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(22.5^{\\circ}\\right) &lt; \\tan\\left(30^{\\circ}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e04dd57c756a737b929ced2bee9aa422bb0308c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(30^{\\circ}\\right) = \\frac{\\sin\\left(30^{\\circ}\\right)}{\\cos\\left(30^{\\circ}\\right)} = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -31px\" width=\"290\" height=\"60\" />.\n</p><p>Thus we need to find an answer choice that is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821ee242c2d18e8db70f539d073b0ace2ddc1301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />, and we also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is wrong since certainly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1636a76c10e0890cc76b13db227c82ad70039b9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(22.5^{\\circ}\\right) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />. The other options involve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" />, which we can approximate using the 'Babylonian method':\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f30604475c2df972ac51b17928f4003a0df03ac0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{n+1} = \\frac{x_n + \\frac{S}{x_n}}{2},\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"42\" />\nwhere in this recurrence relation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1b2737569fde033bbf00c9ee9f7d7ec608ac093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> is the current guess for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e22dabac373a3ad13130474922617e98b6bc0e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdee5e53970edceae79323e26921a8d62d3f76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> would be the next approximated guess. As such, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/e/c7ea4cccbebc01502bbf044e8bb36b8089ad7f09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2} \\approx \\frac{1+\\frac{2}{1}}{2} = 1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"144\" height=\"42\" />, or if you memorized the value then you can take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd081ca18cdc3a8d1399986aa6a2111a73bea546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2} \\approx 1.414$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"21\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> the approximation would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/d/36dcb76116f779f9ce43e147b6f44eefaca69c0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3} \\approx \\frac{2+\\frac{3}{2}}{2} = 1.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"153\" height=\"42\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c9971b5a5d2b17e13497899d2ea722e9fa43fb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(30^{\\circ}\\right) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\approx \\frac{1}{1.75} = \\frac{4}{7} \\approx 0.571$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"287\" height=\"43\" />. Using these values we can check the approximate value of every answer choice (having already eliminated choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> as explained above):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/562cbf820d3b7abba25c92ec784b8398ba071035.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}&amp;\\textbf{(B) } \\sqrt{2}-1 \\approx 1.414 - 1 = 0.414, \\\\ &amp;\\textbf{(C) } 2-\\sqrt{2} \\approx 2 - 1.414 = 0.586, \\\\ &amp;\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\approx \\frac{1.414}{2} = 0.707, \\text{ and} \\\\ &amp;\\textbf{(E) } 3-\\sqrt{2} \\approx 3 - 1.414 = 1.586.\\end{align*}\" width=\"255\" height=\"129\" />\n</p><p>As seen above, only choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> satisfies the criterion that the answer is less than approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe52674b0323236bfaf24c8f799d5d4a16905299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.571$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. (Even though choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> may seem to work with e.g. a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/b/10bdfc583d74e0c6535e7aec271f9e243cbcb3ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}\\approx 1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"21\" /> approximation, it is clear geometrically that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c45e8d26535b346fb6bebf86b3138d6bbf612af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(22.5^{\\circ}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" /> is noticeably different from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/9705ef7f116b18f728198c951693e843c08131c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(30^{\\circ}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, so such a close value can't be correct.)\n</p><p>Accordingly, the answer is indeed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/a/5cab5d93baa1e3389a5dddcf44130996f0176c46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } \\sqrt{2}-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"103\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>~tebby\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Very_Fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Very_Fast)\">Solution 4 (Very Fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Very Fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To start, we need to find out what time of day it is. We know there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/a/37a22728a434a9fae0c07c5f9517b277a5a2d8d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24\\cdot60=1440$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" /> minutes in a day, so we only have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/a/dbaca4b72698be1081b6b4bfe3c8d781853dbd29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025-1440 = 585$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"15\" /> minutes that we care about. We see that this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times with an extra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes tacked on, so the time is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d5519fdc63d96b5aa59714c0755969ed7293846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9:45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, we have the arms of the clock face in this configuration:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f269904d4a1fc197a9d3528855f2c5c5261f65.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import geometry; size(130); draw(circle((0,0), 100)); point A= rotate(-22.5) * (-100,0); point B= (-100,0); point C= (0,0); point D= (0,100); point E= rotate(-30) * (-100,0); draw(A--C); draw(B--C); draw((C--D), dashed); draw(C--E); markangle(&quot;$\\small\\theta$&quot;, radius=9, A, C, B); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(-100,0),W); label(&quot;$10$&quot;,rotate(-30) * (-100,0),NW); label(&quot;$12$&quot;,(0,100),N); [/asy]\" width=\"215\" height=\"218\" />\nThen, since the angle between any two consecutive hours is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b4d5c3424e807c380b0ea8fea926d58f18f7b5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2\\pi}{12} = \\frac{\\pi}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"65\" height=\"38\" />, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d9647f194f46eb054c6d306e3dbcd616302ac1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\frac{45}{60} \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{6} = \\frac{3}{4}\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{6} = \\frac{\\pi}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" /> (which is indeed the <i>acute</i> angle between the hour hand and the minute hand, as required by the problem). Therefore, using a standard half-angle identity, the answer is precisely\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/8770f81724fbf352e3796e284d94d12e413f21ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)=\\frac{\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)}{\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)+1}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}+1\\right)}=\\frac{1}{1+\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{1 \\cdot \\left(\\sqrt{2}-1\\right)}{\\left(1+\\sqrt{2}\\right) \\cdot \\left(\\sqrt{2}-1\\right)}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2-1}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\sqrt{2}-1}.\\]\" width=\"775\" height=\"69\" />\n</p><p>~shockfront99\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FdSkJ-LiZh4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FdSkJ-LiZh4</a>\n~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=22awgqmL2GA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=22awgqmL2GA</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_MadMath\">Video Solution 3 by MadMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 by MadMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZAEuDOAieqs\">https://youtu.be/ZAEuDOAieqs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B\">2025 AMC 12B</a></